iability of the RNA-seq results. The correlation coefficient (R<sup>2</sup>) and linear regression equations were provided for each gene.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="pathogens-14-00485-g009.jpg"><?image-name pathogens-14-00485-g009.jpg?><?image-size 90706?><?image-md5 ffe58dec1c3f517af1c82b8702c7fd51?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 3893?><?image-original-width 4063?><?image-scaled-height 707?><?image-scaled-width 738?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/1aa3/12114223/ffe58dec1c3f/pathogens-14-00485-g009.jpg?><?thumb-name pathogens-14-00485-g009.gif?><?thumb-size 6490?><?thumb-md5 5290511e067ed1c614ac12075322a956?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 96?><?thumb-scaled-width 100?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/1aa3/12114223/5290511e067e/pathogens-14-00485-g009.gif?></graphic></fig></floats-group></article>